Today is Monday morning.
I am standing at the bus stop as usual.
In a short while, my daily bus arrives.
I board the bus.
"Dada, please give me a ticket," I say to the conductor.
The conductor gives me a ticket and I sit near the window.
The bus moves forward along the road.
I look outside through the window.
There is a lot of crowd and traffic on the road, as usual.
Seeing this, I remember the month of January.
When I first came to Mumbai, all this was very new.
Initially, the crowd and the noise of vehicles here felt overwhelming to me.
I didn't understand how to travel by bus.
But now the situation has changed.
This bus journey has now become my daily habit.
Now I don't feel afraid of this city at all.
I know my stops and routes well.
I travel peacefully, looking outside.
Now this city feels like my home.
